{"type":"custom","customType":"clawdbot.cache-ttl","data":{"timestamp":1769987449148,"provider":"anthropic","modelId":"claude-opus-4-5"},"id":"3d88d772","parentId":"02aaff80","timestamp":"2026-02-01T23:10:49.148Z"}
{"type":"message","id":"877c2ff0","parentId":"3d88d772","timestamp":"2026-02-01T23:10:49.149Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a JOC contractor lead scraper for Scout at /home/ec2-user/clawd/\n\n## What to build: scripts/scout-joc-leads.js\n\nA Node.js script that searches for publicly awarded JOC contracts and builds a lead list of contractors.\n\n## Data Sources to Search (via Brave Search API):\n\nUse Brave Search API:\n- Key location: read from gateway config at /home/ec2-user/.clawdbot/gateway.json or clawdbot.json — look for tools.web.search.apiKey or brave apiKey\n- Endpoint: https://api.search.brave.com/res/v1/web/search\n- Headers: { 'X-Subscription-Token': API_KEY, 'Accept': 'application/json' }\n- Rate limit: 1 request per second\n\n### Search queries (run all of these):\n1. \"job order contracting\" \"contract awarded\" 2025 OR 2026\n2. \"JOC contract\" \"awarded to\" contractor 2025 OR 2026\n3. site:sam.gov \"job order contracting\" award\n4. \"OMNIA Partners\" \"job order contracting\" awarded\n5. \"Gordian\" \"JOC\" \"contract awarded\" 2025 OR 2026\n6. \"Centennial Contractors\" JOC award\n7. \"job order contracting\" RFP awarded state OR county OR city\n8. \"indefinite delivery\" \"job order\" contracting award 2025 OR 2026\n9. \"JOC\" \"task order\" contractor awarded government\n10. \"cooperative contract\" \"job order contracting\" public agency\n11. site:governmentbids.com \"job order contracting\"\n12. site:bidnet.com \"job order contracting\"\n13. \"JOC contract\" awarded million OR \"$\" contractor\n14. \"construction task catalog\" contract awarded\n15. \"unit price book\" \"job order\" awarded contractor\n\nFor each query, request count=10 results.\n\n### For each search result:\n1. Fetch the page content using fetch() with a reasonable User-Agent\n2. Extract structured data where possible:\n   - **Agency name** (who awarded the contract)\n   - **Contractor name** (who won it)\n   - **Contract value** (dollar amount if mentioned)\n   - **Location** (state/city)\n   - **JOC provider** (Gordian, Centennial, etc. if mentioned)\n   - **Date** (when awarded)\n   - **Source URL**\n3. Use regex patterns to extract:\n   - Dollar amounts: /\\$[\\d,]+(?:\\.\\d{2})?(?:\\s*(?:million|M|billion|B))?/gi\n   - Company names near keywords like \"awarded to\", \"contractor:\", \"vendor:\"\n   - State names and city names\n   - Dates in various formats\n\n### Output:\n\n1. **Raw leads file**: /home/ec2-user/clawd/agents/scout/reports/joc-leads-YYYY-MM-DD.json\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"agency\": \"Oregon State University\",\n    \"contractor\": \"Unknown\",\n    \"jocProvider\": \"Gordian\",\n    \"value\": \"$2,000,000\",\n    \"location\": \"Oregon\",\n    \"date\": \"2026-01-27\",\n    \"source\": \"https://...\",\n    \"title\": \"Article title\",\n    \"snippet\": \"Brief excerpt with context\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n2. **Formatted report**: /home/ec2-user/clawd/agents/scout/reports/joc-leads-YYYY-MM-DD.md\n```markdown\n# JOC Contract Leads — YYYY-MM-DD\n\n## Summary\n- X contracts found\n- Y unique contractors identified\n- Z unique agencies\n- Total contract value: $X\n\n## Leads\n\n### 1. [Agency Name] → [Contractor Name]\n- **Value:** $X\n- **Location:** State\n- **JOC Provider:** Gordian/Centennial/Other\n- **Date:** YYYY-MM-DD\n- **Source:** [link](url)\n- **Notes:** Brief context\n\n### 2. ...\n```\n\n3. **CSV export**: /home/ec2-user/clawd/agents/scout/reports/joc-leads-YYYY-MM-DD.csv\nHeaders: agency,contractor,joc_provider,value,location,date,source_url\n(For easy import into a CRM or spreadsheet later)\n\n### Error Handling:\n- If a page fetch fails, skip it and log the error\n- If no structured data can be extracted from a result, still include it with what we have (title, snippet, URL)\n- Deduplicate by URL\n- 1-second delay between all API calls\n- Total Brave API queries: 15 (well within daily limits)\n- Page fetches: up to 150, but with 500ms delays and timeout of 10s each\n\n### Also:\n- Create a wrapper: scripts/scout-joc-wrapper.sh\n- Add documentation to agents/scout/SETUP.md about running the lead scraper\n- Make the script importable/callable from the main scout-scan.js in the future\n\n## Test:\nRun the script once. It should produce all 3 output files. Show the summary stats and first 5 leads in the output.\n\n## IMPORTANT:\n- Be respectful of rate limits — no hammering\n- Some pages will be PDFs or login-gated — skip gracefully\n- Focus on getting SOMETHING useful even if extraction isn't perfect\n- The contractor name is the most valuable field — try hardest to extract that\n- This is lead gen, not perfect data — quantity of signals matters"}],"timestamp":1769987449148}}
