{"type":"message","id":"3b776424","parentId":"2e73ffbc","timestamp":"2026-02-01T23:11:15.103Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can't find the Brave API key in config files. Since I have the `web_search` tool available which uses Brave Search, I'll design the script to use that tool indirectly. But wait - the script needs to run standalone. Let me think about this differently.\n\nThe script needs a Brave API key. Since I can't find it in config, I'll make the script accept it via environment variable, and also try to use the web_search tool directly for the initial run/test. Actually, let me just build the script to use the web_search and web_fetch tools I have access to - no, those are Clawdbot tools, not available to a Node.js script.\n\n\nI'll build the Node.js script to accept the Brave API key through an environment variable, then use my available tools to gather the data for testing while keeping the standalone script ready for future use.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01K83BEQHdcB3QVTpRnwwnVW","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find /home/ec2-user/.clawdbot -name \"*.yaml\" -o -name \"*.yml\" -o -name \"*.toml\" -o -name \"*.conf\" 2>/dev/null | head -10; ls /home/ec2-user/.clawdbot/"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":1,"output":408,"cacheRead":12957,"cacheWrite":176,"totalTokens":13542,"cost":{"input":0.000005,"output":0.0102,"cacheRead":0.0064785,"cacheWrite":0.0011,"total":0.0177835}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1769987465153}}
